// JCA/JCE — JDK 24+ built-in provider (JEP 497) KeyPairGenerator kpg = KeyPairGenerator.getInstance("ML-DSA"); kpg.initialize(NamedParameterSpec.ML_DSA_65); KeyPair kp = kpg.generateKeyPair(); PublicKey pub = kp.getPublic(); PrivateKey priv = kp.getPrivate(); // JDK 21 or earlier: register Bouncy Castle and use // KeyPairGenerator.getInstance("ML-DSA-65", "BC")
Built into JDK 24+, JDK 25 LTS and Oracle JDK 21.0.13 / 17.0.21 (October 2026). On a JDK without it, register the Bouncy Castle provider. Algorithm name is string-based.
// OpenSSL 3.5+ — ML-DSA is in the default provider EVP_PKEY_CTX *ctx = EVP_PKEY_CTX_new_from_name( NULL, "ML-DSA-65", NULL ); EVP_PKEY_keygen_init(ctx); EVP_PKEY *pkey = NULL; EVP_PKEY_keygen(ctx, &pkey); EVP_PKEY_CTX_free(ctx); // pkey now holds ML-DSA-65 key pair
Native since OpenSSL 3.5. oqsprovider is only needed on OpenSSL before 3.5 or for non-standardised algorithms. EVP API is algorithm-agnostic.
// PKCS#11 v3.2 — ML-DSA key pair generation CK_MECHANISM mech = {CKM_ML_DSA_KEY_PAIR_GEN, NULL, 0}; CK_ATTRIBUTE pubTmpl[] = { {CKA_TOKEN, &ckTrue, sizeof(CK_BBOOL)}, {CKA_VERIFY, &ckTrue, sizeof(CK_BBOOL)}, {CKA_ML_DSA_PARAMETER_SET, "ML-DSA-65", 9} }; CK_ATTRIBUTE privTmpl[] = { {CKA_TOKEN, &ckTrue, sizeof(CK_BBOOL)}, {CKA_SIGN, &ckTrue, sizeof(CK_BBOOL)}, {CKA_SENSITIVE, &ckTrue, sizeof(CK_BBOOL)} }; CK_OBJECT_HANDLE hPub, hPriv; C_GenerateKeyPair(session, &mech, pubTmpl, 3, privTmpl, 3, &hPub, &hPriv);
Keys stored on HSM token. Handles are opaque — key material never exposed.
// Windows CNG (BCrypt) — Windows 11 24H2+ / Server 2025 BCRYPT_ALG_HANDLE hAlg; BCryptOpenAlgorithmProvider(&hAlg, BCRYPT_MLDSA_ALGORITHM, NULL, 0); BCRYPT_KEY_HANDLE hKey; BCryptGenerateKeyPair(hAlg, &hKey, 0, 0); // Parameter set must be set before finalizing BCryptSetProperty(hKey, BCRYPT_PARAMETER_SET_NAME, (PUCHAR)BCRYPT_MLDSA_PARAMETER_SET_65, sizeof(BCRYPT_MLDSA_PARAMETER_SET_65), 0); BCryptFinalizeKeyPair(hKey, 0);
ML-KEM and ML-DSA are generally available in the default CNG provider; SLH-DSA is defined but not implemented by it. Older Windows builds return STATUS_NOT_SUPPORTED. Use NCrypt with a KSP for persisted keys.
// Bouncy Castle lightweight API (no JCA) MLDSAKeyPairGenerator gen = new MLDSAKeyPairGenerator(); gen.init(new MLDSAKeyGenerationParameters( new SecureRandom(), MLDSAParameters.ml_dsa_65 )); AsymmetricCipherKeyPair kp = gen.generateKeyPair(); MLDSAPublicKeyParameters pub = (MLDSAPublicKeyParameters) kp.getPublic(); MLDSAPrivateKeyParameters priv = (MLDSAPrivateKeyParameters) kp.getPrivate();
Lightweight API — direct class instantiation, no provider registration.
// Bouncy Castle C# — ML-DSA key generation var gen = new MLDsaKeyPairGenerator(); gen.Init(new MLDsaKeyGenerationParameters( new SecureRandom(), MLDsaParameters.ML_DSA_65 )); var kp = gen.GenerateKeyPair(); var pub = (MLDsaPublicKeyParameters)kp.Public; var priv = (MLDsaPrivateKeyParameters)kp.Private;
Identical pattern to Java Bouncy Castle — same API design 
